      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. Locate the main power cable connected to your Zenith Smart Hub unit.\n2. Gently grasp the power cable near the hub itself.\n3. Carefully pull the power cable completely out of the wall outlet socket.\n4. Ensure the connection is fully disengaged from the electrical source.\n5. Set a timer or manually count down sixty seconds from the moment of disconnection.\n6. Wait patiently for the full sixty-second duration to allow for complete power discharge.\n7. Return to the wall outlet where the Zenith Smart Hub was previously connected.\n8. Align the power cable connector precisely with the power socket contacts.\n9. Firmly push the power cable back into the wall outlet until it is securely seated.\n10. Observe the indicator light panel on the front face of the Zenith Smart Hub.\n11. Wait for the initial boot sequence to begin, which may take several minutes.\n12. Confirm that the indicator light transitions from blinking amber to a solid green color.\n13. Open the Zenith companion application on your smartphone or tablet device.\n14. Ensure the application is updated to the latest available version from your device's app store.\n15. Tap on the",
      "source": "target",
